WEBVTT

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.179
There are many books at the library.

00:00:11.351 --> 00:00:17.188
Each book has a marvelous story
that would never happen in reality.

00:00:23.763 --> 00:00:31.763
But when you fall in love, reality
becomes more marvelous than any story.

00:00:56.296 --> 00:01:03.032
Why? Somehow you seem upset
Why? Nandaka ochikon deru mitai

00:01:04.671 --> 00:01:11.373
Voice, my voice. I want it to reach you
Voice, my voice. Todoketai yo kimini

00:01:11.978 --> 00:01:19.942
Things aren't going the way you'd like
Omoi douri ni naranai koto nara

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:28.320
That might happen a lot now, but...
Ima wa takusan attarisuru kedo

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:35.224
Tomorrow, another new wind
Mata ashita wa chigau kaze

00:01:35.635 --> 00:01:38.696
will blow your way
fuite kuruyo

00:01:39.072 --> 00:01:43.737
Spread your arms and let your chest
Ryoute wo hirogeta mune ni

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:47.105
just feel the breeze
kanjiru mama

00:01:47.414 --> 00:01:51.976
No matter what befalls us,
Nani ga osoi kakattemo

00:01:52.252 --> 00:01:55.278
no matter how difficult it may be
semetatete mo

00:01:56.022 --> 00:02:02.587
We'll be all right
Watashi tachi wa daijyoubu

00:02:09.702 --> 00:02:13.900
The Suggestion of Natural Love

00:02:22.048 --> 00:02:24.244
So, what about you guys?

00:02:24.451 --> 00:02:26.385
What do you mean?

00:02:26.753 --> 00:02:28.497
What do you think I'm talking about?

00:02:28.521 --> 00:02:30.455
I'm talking about kissing! Kissing!

00:02:31.057 --> 00:02:32.388
K-Kissing?

00:02:32.525 --> 00:02:36.894
| had my first the other day,
but what about you guys?

00:02:37.297 --> 00:02:41.757
Don't tell me... Could it be
you guys have never kissed anyone?

00:02:42.769 --> 00:02:46.205
Of course, ... haven't.

00:02:47.307 --> 00:02:48.502
Kanzaki...

00:02:50.143 --> 00:02:50.905
What?

00:02:51.778 --> 00:02:55.874
Aren't you dating Nitta,
a barbarian that looks human?

00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:59.416
Don't you think it's a problem
that you guys haven't kissed yet?

00:02:59.786 --> 00:03:00.996
Th-That's...

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.112
Hey, you guys.

00:03:03.223 --> 00:03:05.453
Were you guys just talking about me?

00:03:05.792 --> 00:03:07.536
Um... Well...

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.891
No, well about Kiss...

00:03:09.696 --> 00:03:11.425
No, Kiss... Kiss...

00:03:11.631 --> 00:03:15.329
Right! Is it odds (Kisuu) or evens (guusuu)
that can be divided by two?

00:03:16.469 --> 00:03:22.238
Basically, we were talking about
mathematics. Right, Kenjo?

00:03:22.375 --> 00:03:30.375
The lone wolf... with his life on the line.

00:03:33.386 --> 00:03:41.386
Fights... Are the roars on the Taiko drums...

00:03:42.128 --> 00:03:43.472
What is he listening to?
Fights... Are the roars on the Taiko drums...

00:03:43.496 --> 00:03:44.258
Fights... Are the roars on the Taiko drums...

00:03:46.032 --> 00:03:50.868
| remember him telling me that he's
been into songs like that lately.

00:03:51.037 --> 00:03:53.005
They're a big hit with him.

00:03:53.673 --> 00:03:56.335
Once he's into something, he sticks with it.

00:03:56.442 --> 00:03:57.273
Really?

00:03:58.278 --> 00:04:02.715
It's fine to be into something,
but he gets really into it.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:10.155
The man's road...

00:04:15.495 --> 00:04:16.929
Okay! One more shot.

00:04:17.463 --> 00:04:20.990
He's a great batter and he
looks after the younger players.

00:04:21.634 --> 00:04:23.830
But he moves at his own pace.

00:04:24.137 --> 00:04:26.538
If he wanted, he could
be the captain next year.

00:04:27.507 --> 00:04:33.037
'We made him join when he had
absolutely no interest in baseball.

00:04:33.413 --> 00:04:35.745
We can't have him leave by putting
too much pressure on him.

00:04:36.449 --> 00:04:39.475
Anyway, let's convince him by summer.

00:04:39.752 --> 00:04:44.383
We can't go to the nationals without
him in our Otonishi High baseball club.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:51.927
That's a huge foul.

00:04:52.732 --> 00:04:55.258
I'll go get the ball.

00:04:55.969 --> 00:04:58.199
So, I'm taking a break.

00:04:58.304 --> 00:04:59.328
Library

00:05:08.014 --> 00:05:08.913
Excuse me!

00:05:12.352 --> 00:05:14.878
C-Could I get the ball?

00:05:21.894 --> 00:05:22.520
You...

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:27.022
What are you doing down there?

00:05:27.967 --> 00:05:30.527
Did you see a baseball come this way?

00:05:37.343 --> 00:05:38.936
Th-Thanks.

00:05:48.454 --> 00:05:51.446
Scandinavian Mythology

00:06:17.784 --> 00:06:18.376
Um...

00:06:19.919 --> 00:06:21.011
<i>it's so soft.</i>

00:06:21.621 --> 00:06:23.521
I'm okay now...

00:06:24.624 --> 00:06:25.614
S-Sorry!

00:06:29.028 --> 00:06:30.462
Thank you very much.

00:06:33.333 --> 00:06:36.462
Same here. I was looking for the ball and...

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:39.199
A ball?

00:06:40.139 --> 00:06:41.197
You didn't see it?

00:06:42.241 --> 00:06:42.707
No...

00:06:49.582 --> 00:06:51.277
I'll be on my way now...

00:06:52.819 --> 00:06:53.581
Um...

00:07:13.373 --> 00:07:18.209
Thank you very much. Well, goodbye.

00:07:48.574 --> 00:07:50.474
What's his deal?

00:07:51.043 --> 00:07:51.908
| don't Know.

00:08:39.625 --> 00:08:41.957
The Power of Love
By Reiko Himuro

00:08:50.436 --> 00:08:51.335
Got it!

00:08:52.338 --> 00:08:54.363
Okay! One more shot!

00:08:55.741 --> 00:08:57.903
Kenjo hasn't showed up.

00:08:58.177 --> 00:09:00.202
The meet's coming up too...

00:09:17.563 --> 00:09:20.225
Hey... You're not eating. What's wrong?

00:09:20.733 --> 00:09:21.928
You're spacing out.

00:09:23.035 --> 00:09:26.061
It's great... being in love...

00:09:28.941 --> 00:09:30.452
Did something happen?

00:09:30.476 --> 00:09:31.739
You're not acting like yourself.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:36.847
Will you promise not to tell anyone?

00:09:37.483 --> 00:09:39.042
Yes, I promise.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:44.454
Then, I'll tell you. Well...

00:09:59.105 --> 00:09:59.970
Yoshihiko...

00:10:00.873 --> 00:10:01.396
What is it?

00:10:03.042 --> 00:10:05.636
I'm in love.

00:10:07.013 --> 00:10:09.846
I'm in love with you.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.975
| can't believe I told you.
I'm so embarrassed.

00:10:15.321 --> 00:10:16.049
Me too.

00:10:17.557 --> 00:10:21.824
I've been in love with
you for a long time.

00:10:23.029 --> 00:10:23.996
Yoshihiko...

00:10:37.643 --> 00:10:39.873
Th-That really happened?

00:10:40.413 --> 00:10:45.943
Yeah. And now I know that
love is like vitamins.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:50.312
I'm really happy right now.

00:10:52.491 --> 00:10:55.051
That's so great.

00:10:56.495 --> 00:10:59.487
I'm trusting you as a barbarian.

00:11:00.066 --> 00:11:01.625
Don't tell anyone.

00:11:02.201 --> 00:11:03.794
Okay, I promise.

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:05.569
Good. I'll see you later.

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:12.601
What does he mean, "as a barbarian"?

00:11:22.955 --> 00:11:25.720
Library

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:43.072
<i>Record of the Winds Chapter 3: The
City Where the Winds Blow By Hiiri Mizuno</i>

00:11:52.218 --> 00:11:54.186
Kenjo isn't here again.

00:12:03.496 --> 00:12:04.361
Are you all right?

00:12:13.873 --> 00:12:14.601
Is this?

00:12:17.843 --> 00:12:20.107
Wake up. My hero.

00:12:36.095 --> 00:12:40.089
| see. So that's what happened?

00:12:40.199 --> 00:12:45.638
Yes, she and I were destined to
be together from a past life.

00:12:46.172 --> 00:12:51.235
So, you defeated the Emperor of Darkness
and lived happily ever after?

00:12:51.644 --> 00:12:53.942
Exactly. How'd you know?

00:12:54.313 --> 00:12:55.508
You've got some talent.

00:12:56.615 --> 00:13:00.074
Don't tell anyone. See you.

00:13:02.088 --> 00:13:05.080
| heard he kissed someone, but...

00:13:05.558 --> 00:13:07.492
What's he into now?

00:13:14.934 --> 00:13:16.459
Paradise Lost
By Jyunichi Wakakami

00:13:25.044 --> 00:13:25.738
Out!

00:13:27.413 --> 00:13:29.091
Today's the third day.

00:13:29.115 --> 00:13:31.675
Yeah, it's a long break.

00:14:02.047 --> 00:14:02.741
Sorry.

00:14:03.249 --> 00:14:04.739
No. It's okay.

00:14:04.984 --> 00:14:07.078
It's not okay!

00:14:07.686 --> 00:14:09.245
It's not okay?

00:14:09.855 --> 00:14:13.723
There's no "good" or "bad"
between a man and a woman.

00:14:15.027 --> 00:14:17.496
You think so?

00:14:17.963 --> 00:14:21.331
| guess everyone's been fooling around.

00:14:30.442 --> 00:14:32.672
Kyoichi? What are you doing?

00:14:33.979 --> 00:14:36.311
| wanted to walk home with you.

00:14:36.448 --> 00:14:38.849
Library

00:14:40.186 --> 00:14:43.554
I'm supposed to keep this a secret
but, it's about Kenjo...

00:14:44.156 --> 00:14:49.526
| know about that. It's about him
and the girl in the library, right?

00:14:49.662 --> 00:14:50.891
Who told you?

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.991
He did. Who told you?

00:14:53.199 --> 00:14:54.758
He told me too.

00:14:55.401 --> 00:14:58.462
He told me to keep it a secret,
but he went and told you himself.

00:14:59.038 --> 00:14:59.937
What the heck...

00:15:00.506 --> 00:15:01.337
But...

00:15:02.208 --> 00:15:03.767
But, what?

00:15:07.112 --> 00:15:10.104
I'm a bit jealous... that's what I was thinking.

00:15:10.449 --> 00:15:11.143
What?

00:15:13.452 --> 00:15:20.017
| think any girl would like to
be in a situation like that.

00:15:22.228 --> 00:15:25.664
Is that what a girl likes to do?

00:15:30.035 --> 00:15:35.201
Ch-Chiharu... Do you want to do that too?

00:15:36.508 --> 00:15:38.806
Well... just a little.

00:15:39.845 --> 00:15:41.040
Watch out!

00:15:41.547 --> 00:15:42.514
Kyoichi!

00:15:43.015 --> 00:15:44.540
<i>OW-OW-OW-OW-OW.</i>

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:46.008
Are you all right?

00:15:46.185 --> 00:15:47.914
Kyoichi, you're acting strange.

00:15:48.287 --> 00:15:52.246
It's because you keep
saying such bold things.

00:15:53.292 --> 00:15:54.953
Well, if it isn't Kanzaki and Nitta.

00:15:55.561 --> 00:15:57.928
What are you guys doing?

00:15:59.999 --> 00:16:01.728
A world of swords and magic?!
A world of swords and magic?!

00:16:02.268 --> 00:16:05.966
Yeah, that's the story he told me.

00:16:06.572 --> 00:16:12.807
The story I heard was more like...
A love story meant for girls.

00:16:13.579 --> 00:16:19.575
| see. Kenjo was telling us
completely different stories.

00:16:19.952 --> 00:16:22.546
What did he tell you?

00:16:23.923 --> 00:16:26.415
He told me... Um...

00:16:29.662 --> 00:16:32.188
No wonder you were acting so strange.

00:16:33.332 --> 00:16:34.026
Perv.

00:16:34.633 --> 00:16:35.410
Sorry.

00:16:35.434 --> 00:16:38.165
Are you guys talking about Kenjo, too?

00:16:38.837 --> 00:16:39.633
Aki!

00:16:40.306 --> 00:16:41.364
How long have you been there?

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:46.205
For a while. It seemed like you were
talking about secrets, so I didn't say anything.

00:16:48.247 --> 00:16:50.773
Secrets? The Kenjo stories?

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:51.815
Is that it?

00:16:51.884 --> 00:16:55.377
Yeah, "The Yoshihiko Kenjo
kiss incident at the library".

00:16:56.155 --> 00:16:58.089
He told us too.

00:16:58.524 --> 00:16:59.491
Right, Yumi?

00:16:59.591 --> 00:17:03.084
But ours had a sci-fi spin on it.

00:17:03.329 --> 00:17:04.319
Sci-fi?

00:17:04.797 --> 00:17:07.391
Why are all the stories so different?

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:12.934
So, to find out the truth, I asked the withess.

00:17:13.372 --> 00:17:14.601
What witness?

00:17:15.007 --> 00:17:16.668
He'll be back soon.

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:19.072
There he is.

00:17:20.245 --> 00:17:24.011
He's Minagawa, the witness of this incident.

00:17:24.516 --> 00:17:26.484
I'm Minagawa, the library officer.

00:17:28.153 --> 00:17:29.643
Did you see it?

00:17:29.888 --> 00:17:32.482
Yeah. She's Aya Kurihara.

00:17:32.758 --> 00:17:35.750
She's well known amongst the library officers.

00:17:36.395 --> 00:17:40.263
She came to the library almost
every day in the afternoon.

00:17:40.733 --> 00:17:43.259
She used to like reading books.

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:45.699
She used to?

00:17:58.617 --> 00:18:01.279
Library

00:18:07.126 --> 00:18:11.290
The Turbulence
of the Genroku Era

00:18:12.097 --> 00:18:13.724
Can I talk to you?

00:18:19.671 --> 00:18:21.400
Will it be okay with Chiharu?

00:18:21.907 --> 00:18:25.036
It's better to have a girl
talk about these things.

00:18:26.278 --> 00:18:27.837
She's not coming?

00:18:27.946 --> 00:18:28.572
Right.

00:18:30.749 --> 00:18:35.619
She... Aya was born in Paris.

00:18:37.256 --> 00:18:42.023
She came to Japan for six
months for her dad's work.

00:18:42.928 --> 00:18:50.062
So, even if you wait, she's never
coming back, unfortunately...

00:18:50.736 --> 00:18:51.669
| see...

00:19:00.245 --> 00:19:04.204
There's also something else.
This is hard to tell you, but...

00:19:07.286 --> 00:19:10.017
| heard this from her friend.

00:19:10.689 --> 00:19:13.852
Aya was born and raised in France, so...

00:19:14.393 --> 00:19:18.660
...her communication methods
are a bit different from ours.

00:19:31.477 --> 00:19:37.439
| get it. So that's what that meant.

00:19:43.755 --> 00:19:44.881
Oh boy...

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:04.275
You get a great view of the
baseball team from here.

00:20:06.979 --> 00:20:10.381
Maybe I'll go back to practice.

00:20:14.553 --> 00:20:15.918
Okay! Next!

00:20:17.823 --> 00:20:23.023
Kenjo's batting great for not
being at practice lately.

00:20:23.495 --> 00:20:25.725
Yeah. Seems like he's
really getting into it.

00:20:26.064 --> 00:20:28.260
I'm looking forward to this summer.

00:20:44.383 --> 00:20:45.942
Okay! One more!

00:20:53.325 --> 00:20:56.295
There are many books at the library.

00:20:57.563 --> 00:21:03.900
Each book has a marvelous story that
would never happen in reality.

00:21:12.811 --> 00:21:20.811
But when you fall in love, reality
becomes more marvelous than any story.

00:21:30.796 --> 00:21:33.675
There's no reason,
Riyuu nanka nakute

00:21:33.699 --> 00:21:39.297
we're just happy when we're together
issho nara ureshiku nattari

00:21:40.038 --> 00:21:48.038
Somehow we connect, everyone together
Nanto naku tsuuji au minna ga ii ne

00:21:56.388 --> 00:22:01.417
We lay down on the riverbed
Kawara no shamen nekoron da

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:04.561
stretching our arms and legs
teashi wo nobashite

00:22:05.697 --> 00:22:13.536
Birds flew above our heads
Atama no uewo tori tachi ga tobitatta

00:22:15.007 --> 00:22:19.687
I just look up at the sky
Futo miageta kyou no sora

00:22:19.711 --> 00:22:22.578
it seems to spread forever
doko mademo hirogaru

00:22:23.181 --> 00:22:28.396
All the things bothering me
Donna yuutsu na koto demo

00:22:28.420 --> 00:22:33.221
seems so small
chiisaku omoeru yo

00:22:35.994 --> 00:22:38.840
There's no reason,
Riyuu nanka nakute

00:22:38.864 --> 00:22:44.769
we just sing our favorite songs
sukina uta kuchi zusande tari

00:22:45.270 --> 00:22:53.270
That's the best, that's when it feels great
Sonna toki ga ichiban kimochi ga ii ne

00:22:59.951 --> 00:23:01.663
